I’d like to talk about a time when I needed to search for information for a trip.

It happened about two years ago, right after I had finished my exams. My close friends and I wanted to go on a trip to relax, and we decided to visit Da Nang because none of us had been there before. It’s a coastal city that is well-known for its beautiful beaches, fresh seafood, and many tourist attractions.

We divided the planning tasks among us, and I was responsible for researching natural places to visit. To do this, I browsed travel blogs and online forums to gather recommendations. I also asked some of my friends who had visited Da Nang before, so they could give me useful advice.

I spent several hours collecting information and creating a list of places that matched our interests and budget. Although the process was quite time-consuming, I found it really interesting because I got to discover many new destinations.

In the end, the information I gathered helped us create a well-organized itinerary, which saved us both time and money during the trip. It turned out to be a great experience, and it also taught me the importance of being well-prepared when searching for information.
